{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"symbols","title":"Symbols","group":"Collections & Iteration","order":36,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">A <code>symbol</code> is a unique, immutable primitive used as a property key that can never collide with any other key — and the gateway to customising built-in behaviour.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-plus\"></i>Creating symbols</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const id1 = Symbol(\"id\");\nconst id2 = Symbol(\"id\");\nconsole.log(id1 === id2, typeof id1, id1.description, id1.toString());\n\nconst user = { name: \"Asha\", [id1]: 123 };\nconsole.log(user[id1], Object.keys(user), JSON.stringify(user));\nconsole.log(Object.getOwnPropertySymbols(user), Reflect.ownKeys(user));\n\nconst shared = Symbol.for(\"app.token\");      // global registry\nconsole.log(shared === Symbol.for(\"app.token\"), Symbol.keyFor(shared));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>false symbol id Symbol(id)\n123 [ 'name' ] {\"name\":\"Asha\"}\n[ Symbol(id) ] [ 'name', Symbol(id) ]\ntrue app.token</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--note\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Key point</div><p>Symbol keys are skipped by <code>for…in</code>, <code>Object.keys</code> and <code>JSON.stringify</code> — handy for metadata that should not leak into serialisation. They are <em>not</em> private: <code>Object.getOwnPropertySymbols</code> finds them.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-star\"></i>Well-known symbols</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Symbol</th><th>Customises</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>Symbol.iterator</code></td><td><code>for…of</code>, spread, destructuring</td></tr><tr><td><code>Symbol.asyncIterator</code></td><td><code>for await…of</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Symbol.toPrimitive</code></td><td>Conversion to number/string</td></tr><tr><td><code>Symbol.toStringTag</code></td><td><code>Object.prototype.toString</code> output</td></tr><tr><td><code>Symbol.hasInstance</code></td><td><code>instanceof</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>Symbol.dispose</code> / <code>asyncDispose</code></td><td><code>using</code> declarations (explicit resource management)</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>class Temperature {\n  constructor(c) { this.c = c; }\n  get [Symbol.toStringTag]() { return \"Temperature\"; }\n  [Symbol.toPrimitive](hint) { return hint === \"string\" ? `${this.c}°C` : this.c; }\n}\nconst t = new Temperature(21);\nconsole.log(Object.prototype.toString.call(t), `${t}`, t + 1);\n\nclass Even {\n  static [Symbol.hasInstance](n) { return Number.isInteger(n) &amp;&amp; n % 2 === 0; }\n}\nconsole.log(4 instanceof Even, 3 instanceof Even);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>[object Temperature] 21°C 22\ntrue false</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What are Symbols used for?</summary><div><p>Collision-free property keys (for libraries adding metadata to objects they don't own), constants that can't be confused with strings, and well-known symbols to hook into language behaviour (<code>Symbol.iterator</code>, <code>Symbol.toPrimitive</code>, …).</p></div></details></section>"}